as other businesses in nevada continue  to open osha officials are making sure  they're following health and safety  rules 8 news now reporter kate houston  is live in the newsroom tonight with the  latest round of compliance checks  kate yes sasha this week nevada osha  officials conducted some new compliance  checks  as well as some follow-ups and these are  to make sure businesses are following  health and safety measures  such as requiring masks and social  distancing now on thursday and friday of  this week  osha officials did 187 new compliance  checks  they focused on large and small  businesses such as restaurants  retail outlets and aquatic facilities  overall 87 percent of those  establishments across the state  were compliant now on your screen you  can see a breakdown of these numbers  all of the grocery stores observed were  compliant meanwhile pools were 75  percent compliant  now on thursday osha officials also did  some follow-up checks  100 percent of the 18 businesses visited  are now compliant with health and safety  measures  overall 74 follow-up visits have been  conducted  only six businesses were still  non-compliant  investigations are being opened at those  locations which could lead to citations  since mid-march osha has issued 98  citations  54 of those citations were issued in las  vegas  with an average penalty of 5 800 dollars  more follow-up visits will happen next  week those will be in areas where large  groups of people congregate  and at establishments where initial  compliance was low  now since these observations began more  than 1700 businesses have been surveyed  statewide 80 percent of them have been  compliant back to you sasha
 

